# TypeScript migration

`src/` implementation files are **TypeScript only**. New JS/JSX under `src/` is forbidden. `@ts-nocheck` is forbidden.

## Policy

1. **New files under `src/`** — `.ts` / `.tsx` only. Never add `.js` / `.jsx` in `src/`.
2. **`@ts-nocheck`** — do not add. Prefer real types, boundary `any`, or a single-line `@ts-expect-error` with a reason (see `ts-expect-error-cleanup` rule).
3. **`allowJs: true`** — kept for non-`src` / tooling edge cases; `checkJs` stays off. Do not use `allowJs` as a reason to grow JS in `src/`.
4. **When editing** — improve types at the touch point when cheap; do not reintroduce nocheck or JS.
5. Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

## Out of scope (separate tracks)

- Mass removal of `$TSFixMe` / leftover `@ts-expect-error` from ts-migrate
- Turning on project-wide `checkJs`

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD — add src/features/foo.js or restore @ts-nocheck on a domain hook
❌ BAD — new .jsx "just for now" under src/components
✅ GOOD — new helper as .ts / .tsx
✅ GOOD — line @ts-expect-error with a short reason when a vendor type is wrong
✅ GOOD — eslint ban-ts-comment blocks @ts-nocheck project-wide
```
